# Known-good upstream refs this repo's CI builds against.
# Bump deliberately, in a reviewed PR, when adopting an upstream fix.
#
# These are the v1.1.0 release commits. The previous pins predated that
# release (hif-core/hif-frontend/hif-backend by 15/16/36 commits) and carried
# a backend defect that drops a module's parameter declaration on a plain
# verilog2hif -> hif2verilog round trip, regenerating `reg [WIDTH-1:0]` as
# `reg [18446744073709551615:0]`. See #15.
#
# hif-backend is ahead of v1.1.0: the hierarchical_behavioral test added for
# issue #10 needs hif-project/hif-backend#26, which stopped a structure-
# preserving round trip from regenerating instance-connected nets as `reg`.
# Without that commit the regenerated hierarchy does not compile at all.
#
# Moved forward again to include hif-backend#24 (assignment delays and the
# `timescale that carries them) and #27 (hif2vhdl no longer leaving a design
# unit's file empty), so docs/known-limitations.md describes the toolchain this
# repo's CI actually builds. Full suite verified against it: 9/9.
#
# Moved forward to the coordinated `develop` tuple, so CI actually exercises
# the regression this bump accompanies (#22). Each ref is needed:
#
#   hif-backend  f840f5c -> 2c09a44
#     The one that matters. #22 is only reachable from hif-backend#61/#67,
#     which widened a one-bit value from `0` to `1'b0`; that pushed the
#     enclosing line past the printer's wrap column and split `a & b` across
#     two lines. Held at f840f5c, this repo's CI cannot see the failure the
#     accompanying fix addresses -- which is exactly why #22 was found from a
#     sibling checkout and not from CI.
#
#   hif-core     776fd24 -> 0fc2751   (hif-core#17)
#   hif-frontend 6b23a13 -> 43890f2   (hif-frontend#19)
#     Moved together, not cosmetically: hif-frontend 43890f2 pins hif-core
#     0fc2751 as its own minimum, and this is the tuple the fix was verified
#     against end to end. Pinning a combination that was never built would be
#     guessing at compatibility rather than recording it.
#
# Verified locally against these exact refs: hif-muffin 10/10, with the
# regenerated and2.v accepted by `iverilog -g2005` and simulating to the
# expected nominal / stuck-at-0 / stuck-at-1 behavior.
HIF_CORE_REF=0fc2751d1b4a2fc30fbedb14639e3ede7a6b7433
HIF_FRONTEND_REF=43890f2b9f791252d0d72a41195d48f58d8c211b
HIF_BACKEND_REF=2c09a44f3c5e11d8035cbb6460e5643599f49ca1
